diff --git a/products/logs/skills/authoring-log-alerts/references/threshold-defaults.md b/products/logs/skills/authoring-log-alerts/references/threshold-defaults.md
index 4389df41663d..d486dbf12d71 100644
--- a/products/logs/skills/authoring-log-alerts/references/threshold-defaults.md
+++ b/products/logs/skills/authoring-log-alerts/references/threshold-defaults.md
@@ -49,10 +49,12 @@ When to deviate:
 
 ## `cooldown_minutes = 30`
 
-After a fire, suppress repeat fires for 30 minutes. This avoids paging the same channel every check interval
-during an ongoing incident — once the alert is firing, the user already knows.
+A logs alert notifies once when it starts firing and once when it resolves.
+It does not notify again on each check while it stays firing, whatever the cooldown.
+Cooldown sets the minimum time between any two notifications, so an alert that flaps around the threshold
+notifies at most once per 30 minutes.
 
-Use 0 for snapshot-style alerts where every breach is independently interesting (rare).
+Use 0 when every fire and resolve must notify, even for an alert that flaps (rare).
 
 ## Avoid these footguns
 
diff --git a/products/logs/skills/authoring-log-alerts/references/volume-floor-alerts.md b/products/logs/skills/authoring-log-alerts/references/volume-floor-alerts.md
index ed591cb36c86..998b036eeed8 100644
--- a/products/logs/skills/authoring-log-alerts/references/volume-floor-alerts.md
+++ b/products/logs/skills/authoring-log-alerts/references/volume-floor-alerts.md
@@ -37,7 +37,7 @@ The reasoning:
 - `evaluation_periods: 3`, `datapoints_to_alarm: 3` (3-of-3) — require 3 consecutive quiet windows. A single
   blip won't fire.
 - `window_minutes: 15` minimum — 5-minute floor alerts on noisy services are unreliable.
-- `cooldown_minutes: 60` — once you know the service is quiet, no point re-paging every check.
+- `cooldown_minutes: 60` — a floor alert can flap near the threshold, and this keeps it to one notification per hour.
 
 ## Simulate is essential here
 
